---
// /accessibility/ (rebuild plan Part 5: "Ship a real /accessibility/
// statement"). Each claim names the code or decision that makes it true.
// Keep it true: when a claim stops holding, change the page in the same PR.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base short="Accessibility"
      description="The accessibility standard this site is built to, what it does to meet it, its known limits, and how to report a problem.">
  <!-- Copy drafted with AI assistance; needs MCO staff review before launch (UM AI disclosure). -->
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Accessibility</h1>

    {/* University of Montana policy, WCAG 2.1 AA: rebuild plan Part 5;
        CLAUDE.md. */}
    <p>
      This site is built to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at Level AA,
      the standard University of Montana policy sets for its web content.
      If something here does not work for you, <a href="#report">tell us</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What the site does</h2>
    <ul>
      {/* src/layouts/Base.astro: .mco-skip-link to <main id="main">. */}
      <li>Every page starts with a link that skips to the main content.</li>
      {/* Header theme button, MCO.initThemeToggle({ cycle: true }); theme
          contract in CLAUDE.md: URL, then saved choice, then OS setting. */}
      <li>
        The button in the header switches between dark, light and high contrast themes.
        The site starts in your system's light or dark setting and remembers your choice.
      </li>
      {/* Kit :focus-visible ring (HOUSE-STYLE §5.4); keyboard checks in the
          kit verify harness, run in CI (verify.config.mjs). */}
      <li>Links and controls work from the keyboard, with a visible focus outline.</li>
      {/* src/scripts/photo-hero.ts and src/scripts/search.ts, MCO.announce. */}
      <li>
        When part of a page changes in place, such as the station photos on the homepage or
        search results, screen readers hear what changed.
      </li>
      {/* src/pages/mesonet/{stations,status}/index.astro: <caption>, scope. */}
      <li>Station data is in HTML tables with captions and header cells.</li>
      {/* Status words: src/pages/mesonet/status/index.astro ("Status and
          health are always words; colour carries nothing"). Underlined
          links: src/styles/site.css. */}
      <li>
        Colour never carries meaning alone. Station status is always written in words,
        and links are underlined.
      </li>
      {/* PhotoMosaic alt text "Looking <direction> from <station>". */}
      <li>Station photos have text alternatives naming the station and the direction the camera faces.</li>
      {/* Kit reduced-motion rules (HOUSE-STYLE §5.3). */}
      <li>The site follows your system's reduced motion setting.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How it is tested</h2>
    {/* DECISIONS D17: axe on every PR in all three themes at both widths;
        Lighthouse accessibility budget 100; deploy needs the checks to pass.
        scripts/check-built.mjs (one h1). */}
    <p>
      Every change to the site is checked with the axe accessibility engine in all three themes,
      at desktop and phone widths, and with Lighthouse. A change that fails does not deploy.
    </p>

    <h2>Known limitations</h2>
    <ul>
      {/* Tools are separate repos and hosts: phase-0-report §3.1. */}
      <li>
        The Mesonet tools, the Station Dashboard and the Snowpack Explorer are separate sites.
        They use the same design system and themes. Each site keeps its own theme setting, so a
        theme chosen here does not carry over to them.
      </li>
      {/* phase-0-report §3.2: D³ has no h1, main, header or footer; checked
          live again 22 Oct 2026 (no <h1>, no <main>). */}
      <li>
        The D³ Drought Data Dashboard is a separate site with its own design. It does not yet have a
        main heading or page landmarks, so it is harder to move around with a screen reader.
      </li>
      {/* sustainable-fsa.com/lfp-explorer: Sustainable FSA's own design
          system (phase-0-report §3.2). */}
      <li>The LFP Explorer is part of the Sustainable FSA project and follows that site's design.</li>
      <li>Photo descriptions name the station and direction but do not describe the scene.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="report">Report a problem</h2>
    {/* The footer contact (rebuild plan Phase 1 item 3). */}
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:state.climatologist@umontana.edu">state.climatologist@umontana.edu</a>.
      Include the page address and what you were trying to do. If you need information from this
      site in another format, ask at the same address.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
